or November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>52\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 54\u00b0F, and the record is 81\u00b0F (1999). The low of <strong>28\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"North Platte is setting record highs far faster than chance","p_rec":"If North Platte's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, North Platte has set <strong>68 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 64 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">128 record highs</strong>, far more than the 64 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (59). North Platte's all-time high is 112\u00b0F, on July 11, 1954.","t_chg":"North Platte's nights cooled over the long run. Its days have warmed.","p_chg":"Across 151 complete years: North Platte's average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.13\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.20 to \u22120.07), about \u22122.0\u00b0F since 1875. North Platte's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.19\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.12 to +0.26), about +2.8\u00b0F since 1875.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; 6 months fell. Highs rose in 6 of 12 months.","t_rain":"North Platte has gotten wetter","p_rain":"North Platte's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.21 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.04 to +0.39), about +3.2 inches since 1875. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 21.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 1951 (33.44 in); the driest, 1931 (10.01 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 13 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}